<xml>
  <block type="serial_config" x="25" y="25">
    <field name="BAUD">115200</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Purpose: Use serial commands to attach and detach an interrupt while the sketch is running.
Hardware: use Connections to check pin ownership for your selected board. Open the comment bubbles on the main steps for explanations.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_typed_variable" x="25" y="100">
    <field name="VAR">pulseCount</field>
    <field name="TYPE">uint16_t</field>
    <field name="QUALIFIER">volatile</field>
    <value name="VALUE">
      <block type="math_number">
        <field name="NUM">0</field>
      </block>
    </value>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Create pulseCount as uint16_t. Outside a body it is global; inside a function/setup/loop it belongs to that body. Its value input is the initial value.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="irq_external" x="430" y="25">
    <mutation uid="irq-attach-pulse" />
    <field name="NAME">pulseInput</field>
    <field name="PIN">2</field>
    <field name="EDGE">FALLING</field>
    <field name="INPUT">INPUT_PULLUP</field>
    <field name="START">DISABLED</field>
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="variables_set">
        <field name="VAR">pulseCount</field>
        <value name="VALUE">
          <block type="math_arithmetic">
            <field name="OP">ADD</field>
            <value name="A">
              <block type="variables_get">
                <field name="VAR">pulseCount</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <value name="B">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">1</field>
              </block>
            </value>
          </block>
        </value>
        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Store the calculated value in this variable. Later blocks read the most recently stored value; this is how the program remembers state between steps.</comment>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">This is an interrupt handler. Keep the body short: update counters/flags here and do slow display, serial or SD work in loop. Use atomic access for shared multibyte values.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_setup_section" x="25" y="230">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="serial_text">
        <field name="TEXT">a=attach, d=detach</field>
        <field name="END">println</field>
        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Send this value/text to the computer. A new line finishes one record; same line can build a record from several values. Match Monitor/Plotter baud to the sketch.</comment>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Runs once after power-on or reset. Initialise the program here; repeating measurements and animation belong in loop.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_loop_section" x="430" y="250">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="controls_if">
        <value name="IF0">
          <block type="logic_compare">
            <field name="OP">GT</field>
            <value name="A">
              <block type="serial_available" />
            </value>
            <value name="B">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">0</field>
              </block>
            </value>
          </block>
        </value>
        <statement name="DO0">
          <block type="arduino_typed_variable">
            <field name="VAR">command</field>
            <field name="TYPE">int</field>
            <field name="QUALIFIER">normal</field>
            <value name="VALUE">
              <block type="serial_read" />
            </value>
            <next>
              <block type="controls_if">
                <value name="IF0">
                  <block type="logic_compare">
                    <field name="OP">EQ</field>
                    <value name="A">
                      <block type="variables_get">
                        <field name="VAR">command</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <value name="B">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">97</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <statement name="DO0">
                  <block type="irq_control">
                    <field name="SOURCE">irq-attach-pulse</field>
                    <field name="ACTION">ENABLE</field>
                  </block>
                </statement>
                <next>
                  <block type="controls_if">
                    <value name="IF0">
                      <block type="logic_compare">
                        <field name="OP">EQ</field>
                        <value name="A">
                          <block type="variables_get">
                            <field name="VAR">command</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <value name="B">
                          <block type="math_number">
                            <field name="NUM">100</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <statement name="DO0">
                      <block type="irq_control">
                        <field name="SOURCE">irq-attach-pulse</field>
                        <field name="ACTION">DISABLE</field>
                      </block>
                    </statement>
                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Evaluate the condition first. Execute the enclosed actions only when it is true; otherwise skip them or use the else branch.</comment>
                  </block>
                </next>
                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Evaluate the condition first. Execute the enclosed actions only when it is true; otherwise skip them or use the else branch.</comment>
              </block>
            </next>
            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Create command as int. Outside a body it is global; inside a function/setup/loop it belongs to that body. Its value input is the initial value.</comment>
          </block>
        </statement>
        <next>
          <block type="arduino_typed_variable">
            <field name="VAR">snapshot</field>
            <field name="TYPE">uint16_t</field>
            <field name="QUALIFIER">normal</field>
            <value name="VALUE">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">0</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <next>
              <block type="avr_atomic">
                <statement name="DO">
                  <block type="variables_set">
                    <field name="VAR">snapshot</field>
                    <value name="VALUE">
                      <block type="variables_get">
                        <field name="VAR">pulseCount</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Store the calculated value in this variable. Later blocks read the most recently stored value; this is how the program remembers state between steps.</comment>
                  </block>
                </statement>
                <next>
                  <block type="serial_text">
                    <field name="TEXT">attached:</field>
                    <field name="END">print</field>
                    <next>
                      <block type="serial_send">
                        <field name="END">print</field>
                        <value name="VALUE">
                          <block type="irq_enabled">
                            <field name="SOURCE">irq-attach-pulse</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <next>
                          <block type="serial_text">
                            <field name="TEXT">,pulses:</field>
                            <field name="END">print</field>
                            <next>
                              <block type="serial_send">
                                <field name="END">println</field>
                                <value name="VALUE">
                                  <block type="variables_get">
                                    <field name="VAR">snapshot</field>
                                  </block>
                                </value>
                                <next>
                                  <block type="base_delay">
                                    <value name="DELAY_TIME">
                                      <block type="math_number">
                                        <field name="NUM">100</field>
                                      </block>
                                    </value>
                                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Wait for the given number of milliseconds (1000 ms = 1 second). This pauses the main program; avoid long waits when loop must service motors, music files or serial input.</comment>
                                  </block>
                                </next>
                                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Send this value/text to the computer. A new line finishes one record; same line can build a record from several values. Match Monitor/Plotter baud to the sketch.</comment>
                              </block>
                            </next>
                            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Send this value/text to the computer. A new line finishes one record; same line can build a record from several values. Match Monitor/Plotter baud to the sketch.</comment>
                          </block>
                        </next>
                        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Send this value/text to the computer. A new line finishes one record; same line can build a record from several values. Match Monitor/Plotter baud to the sketch.</comment>
                      </block>
                    </next>
                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Send this value/text to the computer. A new line finishes one record; same line can build a record from several values. Match Monitor/Plotter baud to the sketch.</comment>
                  </block>
                </next>
                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Temporarily prevent interrupts while reading or changing shared multi-byte data. Keep this section short; it restores the previous interrupt state afterward.</comment>
              </block>
            </next>
            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Create snapshot as uint16_t. Outside a body it is global; inside a function/setup/loop it belongs to that body. Its value input is the initial value.</comment>
          </block>
        </next>
        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Evaluate the condition first. Execute the enclosed actions only when it is true; otherwise skip them or use the else branch.</comment>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Repeats until power is removed. Each block runs in order, then execution returns to the top. Keep this loop responsive when servicing motors, music or serial input.</comment>
  </block>
